# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even on Windows checkouts: they are bind-mounted into Linux
# containers (docker/certs, sim/, scripts/) where a CRLF terminator makes bash reject the very first
# `set -o pipefail` line. Learned the hard way while bringing up the 018 mTLS stack.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reason for container/entrypoint and CI files interpreted inside Linux images.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
